<#@ template language="C#" #>
<#@ parameter name="Database" type="CodeGenNew.Core.DatabaseModel" #>
<#@ parameter name="Project" type="CodeGenNew.Core.ProjectSettings" #>
<#@ import namespace="CodeGenNew.Core" #>
<#
    // ==========================================================================================
    // RS_TestUsage_v1.tt
    // Generates: tests/api/usage_<table>.rs   (whole-database; the output folder is the Rust crate's folder)
    // Tests of the usage ledgers (UsageTables) of the Rust API: no token is a 401, a role that is not the administrator's a 403, the summary adds the events per month and kind (and can be limited by kind and
    // dates), another tenant's events are not in it, a platform administrator names the tenant and is the one who records usage, a roll-up totals the old events into the months, and nothing edits or deletes an
    // event. Every Rust test works in a database of its own, so the events need no clean-up. The words are the ones of the ASP.NET tests (API_TestUsage).
    // Written only for a project with RustTests=true, ApiAuth=true, TenantTable and UsageTables; not for SQL Server. Needs Client of tests/api/test_support.rs (RS_EssentialTests); RS_TestBodies lists the modules.
    // Full notes: Docs/TemplateNotes/API_Usage_v1.md
    // ==========================================================================================
    if (RustUsageTests.Applies(Database, Project))
        foreach (var table in UsageTestPlan.Ledgers(Database, Project))
            Write("@@@FILE tests/api/" + RustUsageTests.Module(table) + ".rs@@@\n" + RustUsageTests.File(table, Database, Project, UsagePlan.RollupFor(Database, Project, table)));
#>
